# Schema changes and the node paths that bind an approved contract — contract,
# decision and override nodes — require review by the graph owner.
/specs/schema/ @sb-dev
/specs/nodes/contract-* @sb-dev
# Decision nodes now carry BINDING amendments: the effective contract is the
# approved contract PLUS its selecting decision's grafts and mandatory fixes, so an
# unreviewed decision edit silently rewrites an approved contract's effective text
# without touching the contract file at all.
/specs/nodes/decision-* @sb-dev
# Override nodes are the gate's escape hatch: spec:gate clause (b) waives the
# pr-evidence check on an author-added override, and never authenticates its
# `approved_by` field. Requiring code-owner review on override-* is what makes a
# waiver an independent human approval rather than a self-issued one.
/specs/nodes/override-* @sb-dev
